{"id": "EUVD-2026-107252", "enisaUuid": "04e6593e-9665-3afa-9476-32f04db0c9f2", "description": "In a BIND resolver, inbound DNS protocol messages with a particular structure will result in additional processing, with no limit imposed by BIND.  A DNS message with a maliciously large number of such structures will cause BIND to consume disproportionate amounts of CPU time and memory during processing.\nThis issue affects BIND 9 versions 9.11.0 through 9.18.50, 9.20.0 through 9.20.29, 9.21.0 through 9.21.26, 9.11.3-S1 through 9.18.50-S1, and 9.20.9-S1 through 9.20.29-S1.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T12:41:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T17:19:14", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://kb.isc.org/docs/cve-2026-19630", "https://downloads.isc.org/isc/bind9/9.20.30", "https://downloads.isc.org/isc/bind9/9.21.27"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-19630", "GHSA-53h2-668w-c49r"], "assigner": "isc", "epss": 0.45, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "306fcce5-36a5-38ff-9d52-480df20c5c1c", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.11.0 \u22649.18.50"}, {"id": "7bb71c80-5f0e-377e-93be-1e62d19fe298", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.11.3-S1 \u22649.18.50-S1"}, {"id": "8b88561c-8097-3779-8e98-8dcd7a522912", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.20.0 \u22649.20.29"}, {"id": "8e5ce437-0633-3b7c-97d9-4aa2aa9282e1", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.20.9-S1 \u22649.20.29-S1"}, {"id": "d71d68bd-54a1-3290-b9a1-83d4251b0fbd", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.21.0 \u22649.21.26"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "17725ad8-2eb0-3da4-b3c6-6f344dc7ef0f", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}], "isExploited": false}